NTE|1|L|Description: Aegis Sciences Sexually Transmitted Infection Profile is a multiplex real-time PCR assay used to detect nucleic acid from chlamydia trachomatis, neisseria gonorrhoeae, and trichomonas vaginalis in first-void urine specimens. The analytical sensitivity and specificity of this laboratory developed test meets the validation and test performance criteria as set forth in the accreditation standards of the College of American Pathologists and CLIA regulations.
NTE|2|L|Limitations: Absence of a pathogen does not rule out the possibility of early infection below the limit of detection, interference by nucleic acid degradation and/or the presence of interfering substances, or improper specimen collection. Midstream urine is not recommended for STI Profile testing and negative results should be interpreted with caution. Submit an appropriate sample type if the patient is symptomatic.
NTE|3|L|Lab Disclaimer: Aegis Sciences Corporation has validated the performance characteristics of this laboratory developed molecular pathology test and has established clinical equivalency to other FDA cleared assays with similar intended use. This test has not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. The FDA does not require this test to go through premarket FDA review.
NTE|4|L|These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by Aegis Sciences Corporation. They have not been cleared or approved by the US Food and Drug Administration.
